# L §3.6 look-through, with the binding given `on d` (L §5.7) so it loads.  At depth 1 rule first applies
# (k == 1) and gives owns[p, x]; at depth 2 rule deeper applies and, every stake being 0, each sum term is
# 0 × through[...] = 0 (L §3.2), so through = owns[p, x] again.  owns[a, konto] = 0.5.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind parties
index depths = 1..4

input owns[p in parties, x in places]: num
input stake[p in parties, e in parties]: num
input d: date

def through[p in parties, x in places, k in depths]: num at reader
  rule first = owns[p, x] when k == 1
  rule deeper = owns[p, x] + sum(stake[p, e] * through[e, x, k - 1] for e in parties on d) when k > 1

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  parties + [a, b] lives 2000-01-01..
  accounts + [konto] PLN lives 2019-05-01..
  owns[a, konto] = 0.5
  owns[b, konto] = 0.5
  stake[*, *] = 0
  d = 2026-01-01

ask q1: through[a, konto, 1], through[a, konto, 2] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (0.5, 0.5)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
